  "safe_defer_findings": [
    {
      "id": "C-1",
      "severity": "C",
      "blocks": false,
      "summary": "reports.py's _termination_failed() substring check ('failed'/'failure'/'lost') under-classifies EnvelopeTerminationReason.MINIMUM_STEP_REACHED as non-failure even though its own message states 'without an acceptable correction' \u2014 contradicting the existing D-4 note's claim that the classifier is correct for all known enum members. Impact is cosmetic only (raw termination_status/message are always shown verbatim regardless), so no fabricated or hidden result occurs."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-5",
      "severity": "D",
      "blocks": false,
      "summary": "In run_app(), store_result_action_failure() for a failed flash retry is only set after page.run() has already rendered the Overview body, and there is no st.rerun() on the failure path \u2014 so on the exact run where a flash action fails, Overview shows the generic 'no result yet' info message instead of the specific failure text (which only appears in the sidebar that run, and in Overview on the next rerun). The new regression test only checks that some st.error element anywhere contains the message, so it doesn't catch this ordering gap. No stale/false data is ever shown."
    }
  ],
